            "UI registry must remain semantic and platform-agnostic rather than storing raw CSS or framework-specific style props.",
            "Visual metadata must describe intent and layout contracts, not pixel-perfect implementation details.",
            "Existing registered UI elements should remain valid and be enrichable incrementally.",
            "Metadata should support both server-rendered dashboard HTML and VS Code extension surfaces."
          ],
          "affected_entities": [
            "feature_ui_registry",
            "feature_dashboard_server",
            "feature_vscode_extension",
            "data_model_ui_element"
          ]
        },
        "decision": {
          "chosen": "Extend the semantic UI registry convention to include abstract visual and layout metadata for UI elements. This metadata should describe visual role, density, emphasis, chrome level, layout pattern, alignment, hierarchy, responsive behavior, and state-driven styling semantics, while avoiding concrete CSS values or implementation-specific component props.",
