      {
        "id": "ADR-044",
        "title": "Architect chat must render structured execution artifacts eagerly and normalize multimodal attachments per provider",
        "date": "2026-04-19T21:39:15.402Z",
        "decided_by": "collaborative",
        "status": "accepted",
        "context": {
          "problem": "The architect chat panel had evolved from a stream-only text surface into a structured execution surface, but rich artifacts such as verdict frames, expandable tool traces, pills/chips, and interactive references were not guaranteed to render eagerly. In parallel, multimodal clipboard/image attachments crossed provider boundaries with incompatible payload shapes, creating failures when Anthropic-style image content was sent through the OpenAI path.",
          "constraints": [
            "ADR-006 requires architect chat to use structured tool-calling rather than stream-only narration.",
            "ADR-007 requires preserving the end-to-end agentic tool execution loop in the VS Code chat panel.",
            "The chat webview must remain the canonical presentation layer for execution state, verification state, and tool-use context.",
            "Provider APIs differ in multimodal image content contracts, so translation must be normalized at the provider bridge rather than leaking provider-specific shapes into the UI layer.",
            "Interactive file/entity references and rich execution artifacts must remain compatible with the structured webview model."
          ],
          "affected_entities": [
            "feature_architect_structured_webview",
            "feature_provider_multimodal_attachment_translation",
            "feature_agentic_tool_execution_loop",
            "feature_architect_tool_call_translation",
            "workflow_architect_agentic_tool_execution"
          ]
        },
        "decision": {
          "chosen": "The architect chat panel is defined as a structured execution surface. Rich execution artifacts (including verdict/status framing, expandable tool traces, pills/chips, and interactive entity/file references) must render eagerly at message creation time rather than depending on later repaint/reflow side effects. Multimodal clipboard/image attachments must be normalized in the provider translation layer using provider-specific output shapes while preserving a provider-agnostic UI attachment model.",
          "alternatives": [
            {
              "option": "Keep stream-first rendering and progressively enhance rich artifacts later",
              "rejected_because": "This weakens ADR-006/ADR-007 goals by making the structured execution loop visually unreliable and delaying critical execution context."
            },
            {
              "option": "Handle provider image shape differences directly in the webview or shared UI model",
              "rejected_because": "This leaks provider-specific contracts into presentation concerns and makes multimodal behavior harder to reason about and maintain across providers."
            },
            {
