            "Explorer serves both read-only graph browsing and curated mutation flows from the daemon HTTP surface.",
            "Live updates are delivered via SSE with bounded replay and heartbeat semantics.",
            "Mutation endpoints already require instance-scoped authorization, non-empty reason strings for governed intents, and optimistic concurrency via If-Match snapshot etags.",
            "Explorer must remain safe for graph/cognitive state by funnelling writes through curated intents with audit coverage rather than arbitrary graph mutation."
          ],
          "affected_entities": [
            "dreamgraph-explorer",
            "explorer-readonly-browse",
            "explorer-live-observe",
            "explorer-curated-mutation",
            "explorer-graph-snapshot",
            "graph-event-stream"
          ]
        },
        "decision": {
          "chosen": "Adopt a consistency model where Explorer clients bootstrap from a versioned graph snapshot and then layer live SSE events on top with bounded best-effort replay. If replay gaps exceed the event buffer, clients must refetch the snapshot and reset local derived state. Adopt a mutation safety model where Explorer writes remain curated-intent only, require instance authentication on mutation routes, require If-Match etag checks for optimistic concurrency where configured, and append audit rows for both success and failure.",
