        "id": "ADR-098",
        "title": "LLM-readiness watcher with fingerprinted re-runs for graph bootstrap",
        "date": "2026-05-03T10:27:16.727Z",
        "decided_by": "human",
        "status": "accepted",
        "context": {
          "problem": "dg init may or may not arrive with a working LLM. Default lmstudio/ollama templates have populated env vars but are useless until the user starts the local server and loads a model. Personal templates with API keys may be ready immediately. No current trigger fires the bootstrap chain (scan_project + enrich_seed_data + ADR discovery + first dream cycle) the moment the LLM actually becomes usable, so instances stay on templates/default schema stubs indefinitely.",
          "constraints": [
            "Readiness must reflect actual LLM availability, not env-var presence",
            "Bootstrap must run exactly once per (provider, model, endpoint) configuration",
            "Provider switches must not waste a full source re-scan",
            "Users need a manual escape hatch",
            "Source-file changes after bootstrap need an incremental delta path"
          ],
          "affected_entities": [
            "src/server/daemon.ts",
            "src/tools/scan-project.ts",
            "src/tools/enrich-seed-data.ts",
            "src/tools/init-graph.ts",
            "src/cli/dg.ts",
            "templates/default",
            "templates/lmstudio",
            "templates/ollama"
          ]
        },
        "decision": {
          "chosen": "Add an LLM-readiness watcher in the daemon that fires the bootstrap chain the first time a real completion call against the configured provider returns successfully. Re-run policy: fingerprint = hash(provider + model + url); bootstrap chain runs once per fingerprint. Fingerprint changes trigger re-enrichment ONLY (not a re-scan), reusing existing entity ids and refreshing description/domain/keywords/links. Surface progress via cognitive_status. Add a `dg bootstrap` CLI verb for manual retrigger. Add a debounced file-watcher delta scan for incremental updates after first bootstrap.",
          "alternatives": [
            {
              "option": "Auto-scan during dg init",
              "rejected_because": "LLM config isn't ready at init time for local-LLM templates; would require redoing the scan after enrichment."
            },
            {
              "option": "Poll env-var presence to detect readiness",
              "rejected_because": "False positives on local-LLM templates whose env vars are populated long before the model is loaded."
            },
            {
              "option": "Re-scan on every fingerprint change",
              "rejected_because": "Wasteful — source files haven't moved; only semantic metadata depends on the model."
            }
          ]
        },
        "consequences": {
          "expected": [
            "Instances bootstrap automatically the moment a real LLM is reachable, regardless of when that happens",
            "Provider switches are cheap (re-enrichment only) but still refresh model-dependent metadata",
            "dg bootstrap CLI verb makes the watcher debuggable and gives users an escape hatch",
            "Delta scans keep the graph fresh without a full re-scan on every file save"
          ],
          "risks": [
            "Real completion call costs tokens / startup latency",
            "Fingerprint hash collisions are theoretically possible (mitigated by including url)",
            "Debounced file-watcher needs careful tuning to avoid scan storms"
          ]
        },
        "guard_rails": [
          "Readiness check MUST be a real completion call, not env-var presence",
          "Fingerprint changes MUST NOT trigger a full source re-scan",
          "Existing entity ids MUST be preserved across re-enrichment",
          "dg bootstrap CLI verb MUST remain available as a manual override"
        ],
        "tags": [
          "bootstrap",
          "llm-readiness",
          "scanning",
          "enrichment",
          "cli"
        ]
      },
