        "id": "ADR-124",
        "title": "All persistent JSON writes use atomicWriteFile (temp + fdatasync + rename)",
        "date": "2026-05-05T12:04:18.874Z",
        "decided_by": "collaborative",
        "status": "accepted",
        "context": {
          "problem": "Several CLI commands (attach, export, fork) and the engine-env initializer wrote persistent JSON state with raw writeFile/writeFileSync. A crash or power loss mid-write would leave a truncated or zero-byte file in place of the previous valid state, with no recovery path.",
          "constraints": [
            "No introduction of native fs-extra or graceful-fs deps — use built-in fs/promises and fs only",
            "Sync writes (engine-env init) must also be atomic — mid-init crash must not leave a corrupt instance.json",
            "atomicWriteFile must default to UTF-8 so callers do not have to repeat the encoding flag",
            "Failure path must clean up the orphan .tmp where possible without masking the original error"
          ],
          "affected_entities": [
            "src/utils/atomic-write.ts",
            "src/utils/engine-env.ts",
            "src/cli/commands/attach.ts",
            "src/cli/commands/export.ts",
            "src/cli/commands/fork.ts"
          ]
        },
        "decision": {
          "chosen": "All persistent JSON state writes go through src/utils/atomic-write.ts (open \\u2192 writeFile \\u2192 fdatasync \\u2192 close \\u2192 rename) for the async path. The synchronous engine-env initializer in src/utils/engine-env.ts mirrors the same pattern with openSync \\u2192 writeFileSync \\u2192 fdatasyncSync \\u2192 closeSync \\u2192 renameSync, and unlinks the orphan .tmp on failure. Audit pass converted 8 sites: attach.ts (3), export.ts (3), fork.ts (1), engine-env.ts (1).",
          "alternatives": []
        },
        "consequences": {
          "expected": [
            "Crash or power loss during a write leaves the original file intact and at most a harmless orphan .tmp",
            "Operators can trust that data/*.json files are either the prior valid version or the new valid version, never a partial truncation",
            "New code adding a writeFile against persistent state is an obvious code-smell visible in review"
          ],
          "risks": [
            "Inline sync atomic pattern in engine-env.ts duplicates the helper's logic and can drift",
            "The orphan .tmp cleanup is best-effort; if both rename and unlink fail, the .tmp lingers (harmless but noisy)",
            "Atomic rename is per-filesystem; cross-device renames will fail (mitigated: temp file is in same directory as target)"
          ]
        },
        "guard_rails": [
          "Do NOT add a raw writeFile() / writeFileSync() against any data/*.json or instance.json path — always go through atomicWriteFile or its sync mirror",
          "Do NOT skip fdatasync; rename without fdatasync can still expose torn writes on some filesystems",
          "Do NOT swallow rename errors silently — propagate so the caller knows the write was not durable",
          "When adding new sync write sites, replicate the engine-env.ts inline pattern rather than blocking on the async helper"
        ],
        "tags": []
      },
