      {
        "id": "ADR-179",
        "title": "Provider/model agnosticity: every user-facing fix is applied at provider-neutral seams",
        "date": "2026-05-10T20:20:28.281Z",
        "decided_by": "collaborative",
        "status": "accepted",
        "context": {
          "problem": "A defect that manifests under one provider/model can tempt a fix inside that provider's adapter. Such adapter-local fixes silently diverge user-facing behavior across providers, recur the moment another provider's model exhibits the same pattern, and violate ADR-148's no-branch-on-provider principle. Context: during the v10.0.0 Lattice cutover smoke test of architect-v2, the chat surface leaked raw tool-envelope JSON into a chat bubble, and the same defect can be produced by any provider/model.",
          "constraints": [
            "ADR-140 forbids v1 imports inside architect-v2.",
            "ADR-160 keeps the card taxonomy closed.",
            "ADR-148 pins provider-id branching out of the orchestrator.",
            "The host->webview seam is the only channel through which provider output may reach the user, and only as typed messages."
          ],
          "affected_entities": [
            "architect-v2",
            "architect-v2-cards-render",
            "architect-v2-orchestrator-loop",
            "architect-v2-host-chat-panel",
            "architect-v2-providers-registry"
          ]
        },
        "decision": {
          "chosen": "All user-facing fixes for architect-v2 MUST be applied at provider-neutral seams. (1) Free-text sanitization lives in cards/render.ts as sanitizeFreeText, invoked by renderTrailingNote and renderCompletion. (2) Folding model rationale into structured cards lives in orchestrator/loop.ts via composeTerminalSummary. (3) Live activity ticker events come from a thin ExecutorPort wrapper in host/index.ts that taps every executeCapability call. (4) Provider/model selection UI lives in host/chat-panel/ and reads provider metadata exclusively through providers/registry.ts; no UI code names a provider id. (5) Per-provider state is keyed by providerId but the storage shape is identical for every provider. (6) Adapter-only changes are restricted to wire-protocol concerns and to the static provider profile.",
          "alternatives": [
            {
              "option": "Patch each adapter when its model misbehaves",
              "rejected_because": "Defect recurs with any provider/model; multiplies code paths; violates ADR-148."
            },
            {
              "option": "Centralize sanitization in a shared adapter base class",
              "rejected_because": "Sanitization is rendering, not transport. Bypasses host->webview seam."
            },
            {
              "option": "Add per-provider feature flags to gate UI behavior",
              "rejected_because": "Combinatorial UI states; behavior depends on chosen model; violates the agnosticity goal."
            }
          ]
        },
        "consequences": {
          "expected": [
            "sanitizeFreeText, composeTerminalSummary, and the ExecutorPort activity wrap are part of architect-v2's shared seam contract.",
            "Adapters stay narrow: pure wire concerns.",
            "When a new provider is added, no UI/render/loop change is required.",
            "User-visible behavior is byte-identical across providers given the same model output shape."
          ],
          "risks": [
            "Centralizing sanitization in cards/render.ts means a bug there affects every provider.",
            "ExecutorPort wrap adds a thin layer of indirection on every capability call.",
            "If a future provider returns structured fields the orchestrator does not yet split, the leak path reopens until the adapter is updated."
          ]
        },
        "guard_rails": [
          "Do NOT add JSON-stripping, prose-cleanup, ticker-event emission, default-model selection, provider/model dropdown logic, or any user-visible policy inside an adapter file. Such code MUST live in cards/render.ts, orchestrator/loop.ts, host/index.ts wrapper layer, or host/chat-panel/.",
          "Do NOT introduce branches on providerId outside of host/chat-panel/panel.ts settings persistence. Branch on model.capabilities.api or a provider-neutral capability flag.",
          "Do NOT bypass the typed HostToWebview message seam. The webview MUST NOT receive any provider-shaped payload.",
          "Do NOT key user-facing copy or behavior on provider displayName."
        ],
        "tags": [
          "architect-v2",
          "v10-cutover",
          "provider-agnosticity",
          "rendering",
          "ux",
          "isolation"
        ]
      },
